-- title:
--   A character on the stable Eisenstein torsion of J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq 2$ and $q \neq p$, and let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $q$ in its set of nonunits. Give $J_0(p)$, the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the base-changed modular function field of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar p`, where `HeckeAlg` is the polynomial ring $\mathbf{Z}[\,T_\ell\,]$ indexed by the primes, and write $\mathfrak{P}$ for `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`, the preimage under `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal $(q) \subseteq \mathbf{Z}$. Fix $k, M \in \mathbf{N}$ and a function $n$ on $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf{Q}}/\mathbf{Q})$ with $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^{n(\sigma)}$ for every $\sigma$ and every $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{q^k}=1$. Assume the submodule of $J_0(p)$ annihilated by $(q^k) + \mathfrak{P}^{M+1}$ coincides with that annihilated by $(q^k) + \mathfrak{P}^{M}$, and that the corresponding equality of ideals holds in `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅`, the image of the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $p$ in $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbf{Z}}$ of the integral cusp-form lattice: the ideal generated by $q^k$ together with the $(M+1)$-st power of the image of $\mathfrak{P}$ under `heckeEvalForms p 2` followed by `latticeRestrictHom p ∅` equals the same expression with exponent $M$. Then there is a map $e_0$ from $T := \{v \in J_0(p) : ((q^k) + \mathfrak{P}^M)v = 0\}$ to $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}^{\times}$ such that: $e_0(v_1+v_2) = e_0(v_1)e_0(v_2)$; $e_0(v) = 1$ whenever $\sigma \cdot v = n(\sigma)\,v$ for all $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf{Q}}/\mathbf{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A_q$; and, for $t \in$ `HeckeAlg`, if $e_0(t \cdot v) = 1$ for all $v \in T$, then the image of $t$ under `heckeEvalForms p 2` followed by `latticeRestrictHom p ∅` lies in the ideal generated by $q^k$ together with the $M$-th power of the image of $\mathfrak{P}$.
--
--   This is the dual formulation, for odd $q$, of the rank-one freeness of the étale layer of the Eisenstein torsion tower of $J_0(p)$ in Mazur's study of the Eisenstein ideal: a character on the stable torsion layer killing the inertia-eigenvector part and with annihilator exactly the stable ideal in the lattice Hecke algebra. It is used to prove [`ModularCurve.latticeRestrict_heckeEvalForms_mem_span_sup_of_inertia_smul_smul_eq_nsmul_of_ne_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.latticeRestrict_heckeEvalForms_mem_span_sup_of_inertia_smul_smul_eq_nsmul_of_ne_two), the converse inclusion identifying Hecke operators acting trivially on the inertia-eigenvector sublayer.
-- source:
